// Data and their uncertainties (historical Stage 6, ADR 0002 §5). On the
// smooth affine object X of a model, Calibration<X> indexes the calibrations:
// measured values, each an exact value with a standard uncertainty, of some
// coordinates of X, with their method of evaluation, a reference and a
// revision. Dataset<X> indexes the datasets of a model under a calibration,
// with one coverage factor and at most 64 points. Comparison<X> indexes the
// recorded comparisons of a dataset with the model's exact prediction: the
// fingerprint of the calibration and a verdict, which the kernel is to
// recompute. A comparison whose calibration changed is stale (E_STALE).
//
// An uncertainty here is physical. It never means the rounding error or the
// enclosure of a numerical method. The kernel does not check calibrations,
// datasets and comparisons yet, so this library declares the families only.
pub indexed family Calibration(object(std::geometry::smooth::affine::CInfAffine))
    = calibration constraints(canonical(0));
pub indexed family Dataset(object(std::geometry::smooth::affine::CInfAffine))
    = dataset constraints(canonical(0));
pub indexed family Comparison(object(std::geometry::smooth::affine::CInfAffine))
    = comparison constraints(canonical(0));
